roved": false, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_009"], "suggestions": ["Replace rxn_001 with an explicit cyanosulfidic acetaldehyde-generating subnetwork.", "Set rxn_002 to 3 HCN -> aminomalononitrile.", "Rewrite rxn_009 with H2O reactants and NH3 plus CO2 products, and specify the hydrolysis environment."]}, {"pathway_id": "P5", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_010": 0.86}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.85, "pathway_coherence": 0.8, "environmental_progression": 0.72, "target_achievement": 0.82, "overall_confidence": 0.8, "feedback": "This is the cleanest route in the network and is directly supported by the Ivanov glycine/acetaldehyde experiments. rxn_010 is balanced and reaches the target, but the network should specify the weakly acidic warm aqueous conditions (about pH 3.3-3.7, 60-80 C, no inorganic solids) and acknowledge that threonine is part of a broad, low-selectivity product mixture rather than a selective output.", "approved": true, "problematic_reactions": [], "suggestions": ["Specify pH, temperature, and the absence of inorganic solids for rxn_010.", "Record threonine as part of a broader product mixture and, if possible, include allothreonine and other amino-acid side products.", "Justify the provenance and co-localization of glycine and acetaldehyde."]}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_001": 0.15, "rxn_010": 0.86}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.51, "pathway_coherence": 0.63, "environmental_progression": 0.46, "target_achievement": 0.75, "overall_confidence": 0.58, "feedback": "The terminal glycine + acetaldehyde condensation is literature-supported, but the acetaldehyde-supplying step is not encoded correctly. rxn_001 is an unbalanced shorthand for a multistep UV/H2S photoredox homologation module, and the network does not justify transfer from those conditions into the warm acidic regime that supports rxn_010. This makes the combined pathway less convincing than either module considered separately.", "approved": false, "problematic_