ning caveats are that rxn_009 needs explicit stoichiometry, mol_012 + 2 mol_003 -> mol_015 + mol_002, and the literature is stronger for aminonitrile formation than for environmentally realistic free-threonine release.\",\n      \"approved\": true,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_009\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Rewrite rxn_009 as mol_012 + 2 mol_003 -> mol_015 + mol_002.\",\n        \"Specify UV, pH, CuCN, and H2S conditions for the photoredox step and separate them from the acidic hydrolysis setting.\",\n        \"Annotate threonine/allothreonine output rather than a single stereochemically silent threonine node.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.95,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.78,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.45\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.71,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.89,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.66,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.62,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.7,\n      \"feedback\": \"Coherent route, but weaker than the Cu-assisted branch. Cu-free sulfide photoreduction is plausible in the broader cyanosulfidic literature, yet the threonine-specific implementation is less directly established, and the same neutral-hydrolysis problem remains at rxn_008.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_008\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Rewrite rxn_008 as mol_012 + 2 mol_003 -> mol_015 + mol_002.\",\n        \"Give explicit Cu-free photoredox conditions and justify them from the literature.\",\n        \"Consider stopping the path at threonine aminonitrile if neutral hydrolysis remains unsupported.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_004\": 0.95,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.78,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_009\": 0.69\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0